          Well, the first tournament has come and gone.  I'll admit to many faults, but t'was to be expected when attempting something new.  I knew city guards surrounded the area, but not within the fighting viscinity itself.  I didn't count on troublesome newbies continuously training guards on us however.  I also knew the warrior's guild was nearby.  I thought nothing of them.  I didn't know, however, that they'd have a thing against our friendly Iguanna race.  <br>
          <br>
          Here're the results of the first tournament.  There were 10 contestants.  <br>
          <br>
          1) Dragoons (myself)- 32 Paladin<br>
          2) Folf - 34? Rogue<br>
          3) Tonga - 35? Warrior<br>
          4) Kayain - 34 Druid<br>
          5) Muska - 35 Monk<br>
          6) Gweeda - 36 Paladin<br>
          7) Sorrows - 36 Monk<br>
          8) Markuskorey - 32? Wizard<br>
          9) Bladesinger - 32 Bard<br>
          10) Tinadas - 30? druid (he wanted a chance)<br>
           <br>
          For those of you who wondered why I kept doing random 1-10.. It's because I listed people by their order of sign-up and randomed to see which 2 contestants would face one another. <br>
          <br>
          Bladesinger vs Gweeda ------> Victor Bladesinger<br>
          Muska vs Tonga -------------> Victor Muska<br>
          Sorrows vs Kayain ----------> Victor Sorrows<br>
          Bladesinger vs Markuskorey -> Victor Markuskorey<br>
          Folf vs Markuskorey --------> Victor Folf <br>
          Muska vs Sorrows -----------> Victor Muska<br>
          Muska vs Folf --------------> Victor Muska<br>
          <br>
          Champion of the tournament: Muska<br>
          <br>
          Duels which included myself which did not eliminate people:<br>
          <br>
          Dragoons vs Tinadas --------> Victor Dragoons (Tinadas withdrew from the tournament therafter)<br>
          Dragoons vs Folf -----------> Victor Dragoons<br>
          Dragoons vs Markuskorey ----> Victor Dragoons<br>
          (Final battle) <br>
          Dragoons vs Muska ----------> Victor Muska --- Muska nominated Champion<br>
          <br>
          Problems encountered in the tournament: Spectators were too far away to see who was actually winning and how much damage was actually being dealt. Were they closer however, they might interfere with the combatants.  Bladesinger proved she could kite any paladin or monk or warrior quite easilly.. although it would take probably 2 hours for each victory. No rangers showed up  to demonstrate their snaring powers ;) Half way through the tournament, Muska's friends showed up and lent him their dragon equipment. I was wondering how he and Sorrows were having such an even match, and then on the rematch due to interferrance by the Warrior's Guild Muska ruled Sorrows while barely losing a bubble of life.  On my duel with Muska, I was owned as well.  No chance, no contest, total ownage. *L*  <br>
          <br>
          The second Tournament promisses to be better.  The first lasted WAY too long for the small number of contestants due to newbie interferrance and Warrior's Guild interferrance.  Next Friday, same time (6pm pacific, 9pm eastern.  Come early this time!!) New location.  Official ARENA in Lake Rathe.  All classes welcome.  Restrictions for levels 32-38.  Tanks will not be pinned against the lethal bards.  Dragon equipment restricted.  Please, bring your own gear!  Muska won the last tournament, and I congratulate him for his accomplishment, however.. did anyone really stand a chance against Neku's Cloak of Flames, Dragonbone Bracelets, and whatever other demonic items of power he loaned his iguanna guildmember? <br>
          <br>
          Just come.. have fun! And join in on the festivities.  Contestants will be pinned against only opponents of near level.  So there will be possibly either one or two champions. (example 32 beats a 34, 38 beats a 36, 32 and 38 do not compete against one another)  1000pp reward, same as last time,  for the grand champion(s).  200pp for anyone who bests me. <br>
          Hope to see you next friday!<br>
          <br>
          ~Dragoons~ <br>

